# External User Documentation

This section is for teams publishing documentation to the Developer Portal.
- [Getting Started](./getting-started.html)
- Create a new documentation site - [Create and Publish a Documentation Site](./create-and-publish-documentation-site.html)
- Add an existing documentation repo to the portal - [Add a Documentation Site to the Portal](./add-documentation-site-to-the-portal.html)
- Maintain ownership and quality over time - [Documentation Ownership](./governance-and-ownership.html)
- Offboard content safely when it is no longer needed- [Documentation Offboarding](./offboarding-and-deprecation.html)


## Before you open a PR

1. Make sure the content is written for all users.
2. Confirm ownership details are present (`owner_slack` and `CODEOWNERS`), and review [Documentation Ownership](./governance-and-ownership.html).
3. Run preview and link checks in your docs repository.

## Template repository

Use the MoJ template when starting a new site:

1. [ministryofjustice/template-documentation-site](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/template-documentation-site)
